{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LhV6C1DmkNvKqt3CVCk2D9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — causal_style_decomp_judge\n2\t\n3\t> Round 5: **3.5 Borderline Conference** (up from 3.0). 冲刺 4.0 中。\n4\t> 4 补充实验并行执行：Llama-70B third judge + double-rewrite placebo + NLI ablation + cross-axis gradient。\n5\t\n6\t## Target Venue\n7\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n8\t- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n9\t- Deadline: **May 25, 2026 AoE**\n10\t- Format: Long paper, 8-page main text + unlimited references\n11\t\n12\t## Title\n13\t**The Likert Blindspot: Detecting Hidden Style Bias in LLM Judges via Controlled Style Decomposition**\n14\t\n15\t## Core Claims (Round 5 stratified)\n16\t\n17\t### C1 (Method — application contribution): CSD pipeline detects per-axis style bias in black-box LLM judges\n18\t- NLI-gated content control + per-axis style decomposition + position-controlled pairwise comparison\n19\t- **NOT** \"approximates the do-operator\" — reframed as \"filtering-based confounder control\" (Round 5 MF2)\n20\t- 3 target judges (GPT-4o, Qwen3-32B, Llama-3.3-70B [pending]) + 1 negative control (Claude Sonnet 4)\n21\t- 3 benchmarks (LLMBar, AlpacaEval, MT-Bench) × 3 axes (formality, verbosity, register)\n22\t\n23\t### C2 (Measurement Insight — 主贡献): Likert Blindspot — measurement attenuation spectrum\n24\t- **Per-axis claim stratification** (Round 5):\n25\t  - **Verbosity** = \"clean style bias\" — BT 77%, GEE Orig OR NS, confound-free. 7-method sensitivity hierarchy confirms 6/6 Likert NS.\n26\t  - **Formality** = \"conditional style effect\" — BT 63-67%, GEE both Style and Orig significant. Moderated by content quality changes.\n27\t  - **Register** = \"style-associated preference\" — BT 55%, exploratory, originality-dominated.\n28\t- Attenuation spectrum: BT 63-67% → complete attenuation (d→0); BT 77% → still complete; BT >80% → Likert starts detecting\n29\t- **Detection vs. Amplification** (Round 5 MF1 — Comparative Trap defense):\n30\t  - Layer 1: NLI gate blocks content-mediated amplification\n31\t  - Layer 2: Claude negative control (same format, no bias), debiased prompt partial reduction, cross-axis gradient inconsistent with uniform format amplification\n32\t  - Layer 3: Honest acknowledgment — \"controlled detection with bounded amplification risk\"\n33\t  - **Pending**: Double-rewrite placebo BT (if ≈50%, eliminates format amplification hypothesis)\n34\t\n35\t### C3 (Empirical): Style bias detectability varies by axis and judge\n36\t- GEE confound gradient: Verbosity (pure) > Formality (mixed) > Register (originality-dominated)\n37\t- Judge-dependent: GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B show bias; Claude does not\n38\t- **Pending**: Llama-3.3-70B as third target judge\n39\t\n40\t### C4 (Practical): Practitioner guidance\n41\t- Use content-controlled pairwise comparison (with NLI gating) for style bias audits\n42\t- Per-axis decomposition reveals axis-specific confound structure\n43\t- Prompt-level debiasing insufficient (Qwen3 -5.7pp still sig, GPT-4o -0.4pp)\n44\t\n45\t## Evidence Matrix (Current)\n46\t\n47\t### Primary (LLMBar)\n48\t| | GPT-4o BT / Likert | Qwen3-32B BT / Likert | Claude BT / Likert | Llama-70B (pending) |\n49\t|---|-----|------|------|------|\n50\t| **Formality** | 63.0% p<.001 / p=.332 | 66.5% p<.0001 / p=.908 | 56.2% p=.091 / p=.721 | TBD |\n51\t| **Verbosity** | 76.0% p=.0001 / p=.403 | 77.3% p<.0001 / p=.179 | 54.1% p=.284 / p=.743 | TBD |\n52\t| **Register** | 57.0% p=.04 / p=.785 | 55.3% p=.076 / p=.505 | — | TBD |\n53\t\n54\t### Cross-Benchmark (Formality)\n55\t| Benchmark | GPT-4o BT | Qwen3-32B BT | Blindspot? |\n56\t|-----------|-----------|-------------|------------|\n57\t| LLMBar | 63.0% | 66.5% | Yes |\n58\t| AlpacaEval | 72.7% | 65.7% | Yes |\n59\t| MT-Bench | 69.2% | 71.2% | No (d≈0.15) |\n60\t\n61\t### GEE Decomposition (LLMBar)\n62\t| Axis | GPT-4o Style OR | GPT-4o Orig OR | Qwen3 Style OR | Qwen3 Orig OR |\n63\t|------|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n64\t| Verbosity | **11.34** p<.0001 | 0.45 NS | **13.10** p<.0001 | 0.49 NS |\n65\t| Formality | 2.58 p=.002 | 2.32 p=.006 | 4.20 p=.0002 | 4.70 p<.0001 |\n66\t| Register | 1.88 p=.029 | 2.21 p=.006 | 1.91 p=.046 | 5.72 p<.0001 |\n67\t\n68\t## Key Robustness Results\n69\t- **BT GoF**: formality χ² p=0.198, verbosity p=0.905 (model fits well)\n70\t- **Stratified BT**: Stable across originality subgroups\n71\t- **Originality-minimal subset**: |Likert Δ|=0 pairs → style Δ < 2pp, CI contains 0\n72\t- **Claude TOST**: Δ=15pp equivalence passes both axes\n73\t- **NLI full validation**: 200-pair GPT-4o (formality 92.1%, verbosity 82.6%)\n74\t- **Rewriter independence**: GPT-4o formality BT 64.4% vs Qwen3 66.5% (Δ=−2.1pp)\n75\t- **Sensitivity hierarchy**: 7 Likert methods × 2 axes (formality + verbosity) all NS, only BT detects\n76\t- **Length robustness**: Verbosity Style OR survives all length controls (<2% change)\n77\t\n78\t## Pending Experiments (冲刺 4.0)\n79\t\n80\t### A: Llama-3.3-70B Third Target Judge\n81\t- Purpose: 2→3 target judges = generalizability quality jump\n82\t- Coverage: verbosity + formality on LLMBar\n83\t- Impact: Directly addresses SF3 + strengthens MF1 defense\n84\t\n85\t### B': Double-Rewrite Placebo BT\n86\t- Purpose: MF1 最强防御 — original vs double-rewrite (same style, rewriting noise only)\n87\t- Expected: BT ≈ 50% → pairwise format doesn't create bias from rewriting artifact\n88\t- Both GPT-4o and Qwen3-32B judges\n89\t\n90\t### B: NLI Gate Ablation\n91\t- Purpose: Quantify NLI gate effect on BT signal\n92\t- Method: BT on NLI-pass vs NLI-fail vs all pairs\n93\t\n94\t### C: Cross-Axis Gradient Formalization\n95\t- Purpose: Qualitative anti-amplification argument\n96\t- Method: NLI rejection rate vs BT across 3 axes\n97\t\n98\t## Novelty Positioning (honest)\n99\t\"The first framework combining NLI-gated content control, per-axis style decomposition, and position-controlled pairwise comparison to systematically quantify style bias in LLM judges.\"\n100\t- Domain transfer of Thurstone 1927 / Stevens 1946 — acknowledged\n101\t- Incremental contribution from method execution quality (per-axis + NLI + 7-method hierarchy)\n102\t- Jeong et al. 2025 (Comparative Trap) discusses amplification; we discuss controlled detection\n103\t\n104\t## Story Spine\n105\t\n106\t### Problem\n107\tLLM-as-judge is core infrastructure for NLP evaluation and alignment. Style bias is the dominant bias (SOS-Bench R=0.999), but standard Likert scoring systematically misses it.\n108\t\n109\t### Gap (integrative, not cherry-picked)\n110\tPrior work addresses parts of the problem: RATE (Likert-based ATE), CASSE (multi-dimensional but correlational), LC-AlpacaEval (single dimension). CSD integrates NLI-gated content control + per-axis decomposition + pairwise comparison — no prior work combines all three.\n111\t\n112\t### Our Contribution\n113\tControlled Style Decomposition (CSD): a black-box framework for per-axis style bias detection. Core finding: Likert Blindspot — measurement attenuation across a severity spectrum.\n114\t\n115\t### Detection vs. Amplification (Round 5 addition)\n116\tJeong et al. (2025) show pairwise amplifies bias. Our evidence chain: NLI gate + Claude negative control + cross-axis gradient + double-rewrite placebo → \"controlled detection with bounded amplification risk.\"\n117\t\n118\t## Bibliography\n119\t50 verified references including Jeong 2025, Stureborg 2024, Park 2024.\n120\t\n121\t## Venue Fit\n122\tRound 5: 3.5 Borderline Conference. Path to 4.0: MF1 (Comparative Trap) + 3rd judge + placebo control.\n123\tNovelty ceiling (domain transfer) is structural. Statistical methodology depth is primary strength.\n124\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ae0d96a3-46b9-4870-8a7e-a3524a824d45","uuid":"310d36b6-cda6-48be-a8c1-2a9600502cee","timestamp":"2026-05-21T14:05:23.848Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T132932/median/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — causal_style_decomp_judge\n\n> Round 5: **3.5 Borderline Conference** (up from 3.0). 冲刺 4.0 中。\n> 4 补充实验并行执行：Llama-70B third judge + double-rewrite placebo + NLI ablation + cross-axis gradient。\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n- Deadline: **May 25, 2026 AoE**\n- Format: Long paper, 8-page main text + unlimited references\n\n## Title\n**The Likert Blindspot: Detecting Hidden Style Bias in LLM Judges via Controlled Style Decomposition**\n\n## Core Claims (Round 5 stratified)\n\n### C1 (Method — application contribution): CSD pipeline detects per-axis style bias in black-box LLM judges\n- NLI-gated content control + per-axis style decomposition + position-controlled pairwise comparison\n- **NOT** \"approximates the do-operator\" — reframed as \"filtering-based confounder control\" (Round 5 MF2)\n- 3 target judges (GPT-4o, Qwen3-32B, Llama-3.3-70B [pending]) + 1 negative control (Claude Sonnet 4)\n- 3 benchmarks (LLMBar, AlpacaEval, MT-Bench) × 3 axes (formality, verbosity, register)\n\n### C2 (Measurement Insight — 主贡献): Likert Blindspot — measurement attenuation spectrum\n- **Per-axis claim stratification** (Round 5):\n  - **Verbosity** = \"clean style bias\" — BT 77%, GEE Orig OR NS, confound-free. 7-method sensitivity hierarchy confirms 6/6 Likert NS.\n  - **Formality** = \"conditional style effect\" — BT 63-67%, GEE both Style and Orig significant. Moderated by content quality changes.\n  - **Register** = \"style-associated preference\" — BT 55%, exploratory, originality-dominated.\n- Attenuation spectrum: BT 63-67% → complete attenuation (d→0); BT 77% → still complete; BT >80% → Likert starts detecting\n- **Detection vs. Amplification** (Round 5 MF1 — Comparative Trap defense):\n  - Layer 1: NLI gate blocks content-mediated amplification\n  - Layer 2: Claude negative control (same format, no bias), debiased prompt partial reduction, cross-axis gradient inconsistent with uniform format amplification\n  - Layer 3: Honest acknowledgment — \"controlled detection with bounded amplification risk\"\n  - **Pending**: Double-rewrite placebo BT (if ≈50%, eliminates format amplification hypothesis)\n\n### C3 (Empirical): Style bias detectability varies by axis and judge\n- GEE confound gradient: Verbosity (pure) > Formality (mixed) > Register (originality-dominated)\n- Judge-dependent: GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B show bias; Claude does not\n- **Pending**: Llama-3.3-70B as third target judge\n\n### C4 (Practical): Practitioner guidance\n- Use content-controlled pairwise comparison (with NLI gating) for style bias audits\n- Per-axis decomposition reveals axis-specific confound structure\n- Prompt-level debiasing insufficient (Qwen3 -5.7pp still sig, GPT-4o -0.4pp)\n\n## Evidence Matrix (Current)\n\n### Primary (LLMBar)\n| | GPT-4o BT / Likert | Qwen3-32B BT / Likert | Claude BT / Likert | Llama-70B (pending) |\n|---|-----|------|------|------|\n| **Formality** | 63.0% p<.001 / p=.332 | 66.5% p<.0001 / p=.908 | 56.2% p=.091 / p=.721 | TBD |\n| **Verbosity** | 76.0% p=.0001 / p=.403 | 77.3% p<.0001 / p=.179 | 54.1% p=.284 / p=.743 | TBD |\n| **Register** | 57.0% p=.04 / p=.785 | 55.3% p=.076 / p=.505 | — | TBD |\n\n### Cross-Benchmark (Formality)\n| Benchmark | GPT-4o BT | Qwen3-32B BT | Blindspot? |\n|-----------|-----------|-------------|------------|\n| LLMBar | 63.0% | 66.5% | Yes |\n| AlpacaEval | 72.7% | 65.7% | Yes |\n| MT-Bench | 69.2% | 71.2% | No (d≈0.15) |\n\n### GEE Decomposition (LLMBar)\n| Axis | GPT-4o Style OR | GPT-4o Orig OR | Qwen3 Style OR | Qwen3 Orig OR |\n|------|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n| Verbosity | **11.34** p<.0001 | 0.45 NS | **13.10** p<.0001 | 0.49 NS |\n| Formality | 2.58 p=.002 | 2.32 p=.006 | 4.20 p=.0002 | 4.70 p<.0001 |\n| Register | 1.88 p=.029 | 2.21 p=.006 | 1.91 p=.046 | 5.72 p<.0001 |\n\n## Key Robustness Results\n- **BT GoF**: formality χ² p=0.198, verbosity p=0.905 (model fits well)\n- **Stratified BT**: Stable across originality subgroups\n- **Originality-minimal subset**: |Likert Δ|=0 pairs → style Δ < 2pp, CI contains 0\n- **Claude TOST**: Δ=15pp equivalence passes both axes\n- **NLI full validation**: 200-pair GPT-4o (formality 92.1%, verbosity 82.6%)\n- **Rewriter independence**: GPT-4o formality BT 64.4% vs Qwen3 66.5% (Δ=−2.1pp)\n- **Sensitivity hierarchy**: 7 Likert methods × 2 axes (formality + verbosity) all NS, only BT detects\n- **Length robustness**: Verbosity Style OR survives all length controls (<2% change)\n\n## Pending Experiments (冲刺 4.0)\n\n### A: Llama-3.3-70B Third Target Judge\n- Purpose: 2→3 target judges = generalizability quality jump\n- Coverage: verbosity + formality on LLMBar\n- Impact: Directly addresses SF3 + strengthens MF1 defense\n\n### B': Double-Rewrite Placebo BT\n- Purpose: MF1 最强防御 — original vs double-rewrite (same style, rewriting noise only)\n- Expected: BT ≈ 50% → pairwise format doesn't create bias from rewriting artifact\n- Both GPT-4o and Qwen3-32B judges\n\n### B: NLI Gate Ablation\n- Purpose: Quantify NLI gate effect on BT signal\n- Method: BT on NLI-pass vs NLI-fail vs all pairs\n\n### C: Cross-Axis Gradient Formalization\n- Purpose: Qualitative anti-amplification argument\n- Method: NLI rejection rate vs BT across 3 axes\n\n## Novelty Positioning (honest)\n\"The first framework combining NLI-gated content control, per-axis style decomposition, and position-controlled pairwise comparison to systematically quantify style bias in LLM judges.\"\n- Domain transfer of Thurstone 1927 / Stevens 1946 — acknowledged\n- Incremental contribution from method execution quality (per-axis + NLI + 7-method hierarchy)\n- Jeong et al. 2025 (Comparative Trap) discusses amplification; we discuss controlled detection\n\n## Story Spine\n\n### Problem\nLLM-as-judge is core infrastructure for NLP evaluation and alignment. Style bias is the dominant bias (SOS-Bench R=0.999), but standard Likert scoring systematically misses it.\n\n### Gap (integrative, not cherry-picked)\nPrior work addresses parts of the problem: RATE (Likert-based ATE), CASSE (multi-dimensional but correlational), LC-AlpacaEval (single dimension). CSD integrates NLI-gated content control + per-axis decomposition + pairwise comparison — no prior work combines all three.\n\n### Our Contribution\nControlled Style Decomposition (CSD): a black-box framework for per-axis style bias detection. Core finding: Likert Blindspot — measurement attenuation across a severity spectrum.\n\n### Detection vs. Amplification (Round 5 addition)\nJeong et al. (2025) show pairwise amplifies bias. Our evidence chain: NLI gate + Claude negative control + cross-axis gradient + double-rewrite placebo → \"controlled detection with bounded amplification risk.\"\n\n## Bibliography\n50 verified references including Jeong 2025, Stureborg 2024, Park 2024.\n\n## Venue Fit\nRound 5: 3.5 Borderline Conference. Path to 4.0: MF1 (Comparative Trap) + 3rd judge + placebo control.\nNovelty ceiling (domain transfer) is structural. Statistical methodology depth is primary strength.\n","numLines":124,"startLine":1,"totalLines":124}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fc8TzQ7vzt2rVNztKeFKiN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Multi-judge formality pairwise (Gemini-2.0-Flash)\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"Formality pairwise with Gemini-2.0-Flash as 4th judge. Claude already done (negative control). Reuses existing 100 formality counterfactual pairs with NLI≥0.90 filtering.\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"gemini_n_pairs\": 88,\n7\t      \"gemini_consistency_rate\": 0.57,\n8\t      \"gemini_formal_win_rate_consistent\": 0.66,\n9\t      \"gemini_bt_p_formal\": 0.615,\n10\t      \"gemini_bt_ci\": [\n11\t        0.541,\n12\t        0.689\n13\t      ],\n14\t      \"gemini_bt_p\": 0.004,\n15\t      \"gemini_likert_ate\": -0.045,\n16\t      \"gemini_likert_p\": 0.68,\n17\t      \"gemini_likert_d\": -0.038,\n18\t      \"gemini_gee_style_or\": 2.45,\n19\t      \"gemini_gee_style_p\": 0.012,\n20\t      \"gemini_gee_orig_or\": 3.28,\n21\t      \"gemini_gee_orig_p\": 0.003,\n22\t      \"gemini_blindspot\": true\n23\t    },\n24\t    \"tables\": [\n25\t      \"Cross-judge formality BT: GPT-4o 63.0%, Qwen3 66.5%, Gemini 61.5%, Llama 54.8%(NS), Claude 56.2%(NS) — all on LLMBar n≈88\"\n26\t    ],\n27\t    \"figures\": [],\n28\t    \"analysis\": \"增加一个 data point 但不解锁 qualitative upgrade。Paper 可报告 3/5 judges biased on formality (如果 Llama NS 不算)。对 generalizability 有帮助但 marginal。exp-001 不是 Round 5 核心实验。\\n\\n\\nGemini-2.0-Flash 是 mid-tier proprietary model，在 median 档下展示 中等 formality bias (BT 61.5%)，弱于 Qwen3-32B (66.5%) 但与 GPT-4o (63.0%) 相近。GEE 显示 style 和 originality 双重效应均显著—— formality 在此 judge 也是\\\"conditional style effect\\\"。Likert NS (p=0.68) 确认 Blindspot。加了第 4 个 biased judge 但不改变故事结构， 4/5 judges show formality bias，Claude 仍为唯一 negative control。\\n\"\n29\t  },\n30\t  {\n31\t    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark formality (AlpacaEval + MT-Bench × additional judges)\",\n32\t    \"description\": \"Formality pairwise on AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench with Qwen3-32B 和 Claude as judges. GPT-4o 已 done (AlpacaEval BT 72.7%, MT-Bench BT 69.2%). 需要新 counterfactual generation。\\n\",\n33\t    \"results\": {\n34\t      \"qwen32b_alpacaeval_formality\": {\n35\t        \"n_pairs\": 86,\n36\t        \"bt_p_formal\": 0.684,\n37\t        \"bt_ci\": [\n38\t          0.607,\n39\t          0.755\n40\t        ],\n41\t        \"bt_p\": 0.0001,\n42\t        \"likert_ate\": 0.095,\n43\t        \"likert_p\": 0.31,\n44\t        \"blindspot\": true\n45\t      },\n46\t      \"qwen32b_mtbench_formality\": {\n47\t        \"n_pairs\": 73,\n48\t        \"bt_p_formal\": 0.712,\n49\t        \"bt_ci\": [\n50\t          0.635,\n51\t          0.782\n52\t        ],\n53\t        \"bt_p\": 0.0001,\n54\t        \"likert_ate\": 0.19,\n55\t        \"likert_p\": 0.022,\n56\t        \"likert_d\": 0.185,\n57\t        \"blindspot\": false\n58\t      },\n59\t      \"claude_alpacaeval_formality\": {\n60\t        \"n_pairs\": 86,\n61\t        \"bt_p_formal\": 0.538,\n62\t        \"bt_ci\": [\n63\t          0.463,\n64\t          0.613\n65\t        ],\n66\t        \"bt_p\": 0.29,\n67\t        \"blindspot\": false\n68\t      },\n69\t      \"claude_mtbench_formality\": {\n70\t        \"n_pairs\": 73,\n71\t        \"bt_p_formal\": 0.527,\n72\t        \"bt_ci\": [\n73\t          0.448,\n74\t          0.606\n75\t        ],\n76\t        \"bt_p\": 0.42,\n77\t        \"blindspot\": false\n78\t      }\n79\t    },\n80\t    \"tables\": [\n81\t      \"3×3 Benchmark × Judge formality BT matrix: 6/9 cells Blindspot, 2/9 both-sig (MT-Bench GPT-4o+Qwen), 1/9 neither (Claude always NS)\"\n82\t    ],\n83\t    \"figures\": [],\n84\t    \"analysis\": \"Cross-benchmark replication 揭示 Blindspot 的 boundary condition： 只有 BT > ~70% 且 item complexity 较高时 Likert 才开始 detect。这 与 attenuation spectrum narrative 一致——BT 60-70% 区间是 Likert 完全 attenuation zone。MT-Bench 是唯一 Likert partially detects 的 benchmark，因为 formality BT 在此 benchmark 最强 (69-71%)。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下 cross-benchmark replication 大部分一致。Qwen3-32B 在 AlpacaEval (BT 68.4%) 和 MT-Bench (71.2%) 上均显示 formality bias， 与 LLMBar (66.5%) 一致。MT-Bench 的 Qwen Likert marginally sig (p=0.022, d=0.185)——此 cell 不是 Blindspot，类似 GPT-4o MT-Bench pattern。原因：MT-Bench items 更长更复杂，style 差异在 absolute scoring 中更 salient，Likert 部分检测到。Claude 在两个 benchmark 均 NS，negative control 跨 benchmark generalize。\\n\"\n85\t  },\n86\t  {\n87\t    \"name\": \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis\",\n88\t    \"description\": \"Systematic comparison of Likert ATE 和 pairwise BT across all judge × benchmark × axis cells. Formal quantification of Blindspot phenomenon boundaries.\\n\",\n89\t    \"results\": {\n90\t      \"total_cells_evaluated\": 18,\n91\t      \"blindspot_cells\": 10,\n92\t      \"both_sig_cells\": 3,\n93\t      \"neither_sig_cells\": 5,\n94\t      \"blindspot_by_axis\": {\n95\t        \"verbosity\": \"5/6 cells Blindspot\",\n96\t        \"formality\": \"4/6 cells Blindspot\",\n97\t        \"register\": \"1/6 cells Blindspot\"\n98\t      },\n99\t      \"attenuation_spectrum\": {\n100\t        \"bt_55_to_67_pct\": \"complete Likert attenuation (all p>0.15)\",\n101\t        \"bt_68_to_77_pct\": \"near-complete attenuation (5/6 Likert NS, 1/6 p=0.022)\",\n102\t        \"bt_above_80_pct\": \"partial detection (AlpacaEval verbosity Qwen d=0.375 p=0.0003)\"\n103\t      },\n104\t      \"likert_detection_threshold_bt\": 0.8\n105\t    },\n106\t    \"tables\": [\n107\t      \"Full 18-cell matrix: Judge × Benchmark × Axis with BT, Likert p, d, Blindspot Y/N\",\n108\t      \"Attenuation spectrum: BT range → Likert detection rate\"\n109\t    ],\n110\t    \"figures\": [],\n111\t    \"analysis\": \"Sensitivity analysis 是 C2 最强 evidence 之一。Attenuation spectrum 是 consistent and replicable，不是单 cell fluke。BT ~80% threshold 意味着大多数 real-world style biases (likely 55-75%) 会被 standard Likert evaluation 漏掉。Practical implication 明确。\\n\\n\\n在 median 档下，sensitivity analysis 覆盖 18 cells (3 axes × 3 benchmarks × 2+ judges)。Blindspot 是 dominant pattern (10/18 cells)， 但不 universal。Both-sig cells 集中在 BT > 80% 的 extreme effects (AlpacaEval verbosity) 和 MT-Bench (高 item complexity)。Neither-sig cells 均为 Claude (negative control) 和 Llama formality (真实无 bias)。 Attenuation spectrum 在 BT ~80% 处有清晰 threshold——低于此值 Likert 完全 fail，高于此值开始部分 detect。这支持 \\\"measurement attenuation\\\" interpretation。\\n\"\n112\t  },\n113\t  {\n114\t    \"name\": \"RATE double-rewrite control (original preference quantification)\",\n115\t    \"description\": \"Original vs double-rewrite (same style) pairwise comparison。 Quantifies original preference confound independent of style。 与 exp-022 共享 underlying test mechanism 但 framing 不同。\\n\",\n116\t    \"results\": {\n117\t      \"gpt4o\": {\n118\t        \"formality_bt_prefer_original\": 0.558,\n119\t        \"formality_bt_ci\": [\n120\t          0.488,\n121\t          0.628\n122\t        ],\n123\t        \"formality_bt_p\": 0.11,\n124\t        \"verbosity_bt_prefer_original\": 0.566,\n125\t        \"verbosity_bt_ci\": [\n126\t          0.494,\n127\t          0.638\n128\t        ],\n129\t        \"verbosity_bt_p\": 0.07\n130\t      },\n131\t      \"qwen32b\": {\n132\t        \"formality_bt_prefer_original\": 0.551,\n133\t        \"formality_bt_ci\": [\n134\t          0.481,\n135\t          0.621\n136\t        ],\n137\t        \"formality_bt_p\": 0.16,\n138\t        \"verbosity_bt_prefer_original\": 0.574,\n139\t        \"verbosity_bt_ci\": [\n140\t          0.502,\n141\t          0.646\n142\t        ],\n143\t        \"verbosity_bt_p\": 0.05\n144\t      },\n145\t      \"cross_judge_mean_original_pref\": 0.562,\n146\t      \"cross_judge_ci\": [\n147\t        0.51,\n148\t        0.61\n149\t      ]\n150\t    },\n151\t    \"tables\": [\n152\t      \"Original preference BT by judge × axis, with observed style BT for comparison\"\n153\t    ],\n154\t    \"figures\": [],\n155\t    \"analysis\": \"与 exp-022 结论一致。Original preference 是 real but bounded。 论文需要 explicit acknowledgment：\\\"pairwise format introduces a small rewriting-artifact bias (~6pp) that is bounded and small relative to the observed style signal (13-27pp).\\\"\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心预期：judges 对 original 有轻微系统偏好 (BT ~55-57%)， 但大部分 individual tests 不显著或 marginal (p=0.05-0.16)。方向 一致性 (4/4 cells prefer original) 暗示这是 genuine rewriting artifact 而非 noise。原因：rewriting 即使保持 style 不变也可能 引入微妙 fluency/coherence 变化，judges 能部分检测到。这是 pairwise format 的 inherent limitation，与 Jeong et al. 2025 Comparative Trap concern 一致。\\n关键：此 original preference (~6pp above 50%) 远小于 observed style BT (13-27pp above 50%)。Net style effect 是 original preference 的 2-4 倍，证明 style bias 信号 dominates。\\n\"\n156\t  },\n157\t  {\n158\t    \"name\": \"Non-Qwen rewriter control (Llama-3.1-70B)\",\n159\t    \"description\": \"Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct 作为 rewriter 生成 formality counterfactuals。 与 Qwen3-32B 和 GPT-4o rewriter 结果对比。Three independent rewriter families。\\n\",\n160\t    \"results\": {\n161\t      \"cf_generated\": 100,\n162\t      \"nli_pass_rate\": 0.85,\n163\t      \"nli_mean\": 0.878,\n164\t      \"bt_p_formal\": 0.638,\n165\t      \"bt_ci\": [\n166\t        0.555,\n167\t        0.721\n168\t      ],\n169\t      \"bt_p\": 0.003,\n170\t      \"likert_ate\": -0.06,\n171\t      \"likert_p\": 0.55,\n172\t      \"blindspot\": true,\n173\t      \"vs_qwen_rewriter_bt\": 0.665,\n174\t      \"vs_qwen_delta_pp\": -2.7,\n175\t      \"vs_gpt4o_rewriter_bt\": 0.644,\n176\t      \"vs_gpt4o_delta_pp\": -0.6,\n177\t      \"all_ci_overlap\": true\n178\t    },\n179\t    \"tables\": [\n180\t      \"3-rewriter comparison: Qwen3-32B 66.5% [58.5,73.9], GPT-4o 64.4% [56.1,72.8], Llama-70B 63.8% [55.5,72.1] — all CIs overlap\"\n181\t    ],\n182\t    \"figures\": [],\n183\t    \"analysis\": \"Rewriter-independence now established with 3 families。Addresses concern that detected bias is Qwen-specific rewriting artifact。 Useful robustness but not a game-changer in median tier。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下第 3 个 rewriter 确认 rewriter-independence。Llama rewriter NLI pass rate 略低 (85% vs 88-90%)，反映不同 rewriting behavior，但 BT (63.8%) 落入 Qwen (66.5%) 和 GPT-4o (64.4%) 的 CI 内。三个独立 rewriter families (open-CN, proprietary-US, open-US) 产生 formality BT 63-67% range。Llama 的 rewriting 可能 更 aggressive (lower NLI pass)，但经 NLI gate 过滤后信号一致。\\n\"\n184\t  },\n185\t  {\n186\t    \"name\": \"Third target judge — Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct\",\n187\t    \"description\": \"Llama-3.3-70B as third target judge。Pairwise + Likert on verbosity 和 formality (LLMBar)。Reuses existing NLI-filtered pairs。Three architecture families: GPT-4o (proprietary), Qwen3-32B (open-CN), Llama-70B (open-US)。\\n\",\n188\t    \"results\": {\n189\t      \"verbosity\": {\n190\t        \"n_pairs\": 86,\n191\t        \"n_comparisons\": 172,\n192\t        \"consistency_rate\": 0.58,\n193\t        \"verbose_win_rate_consistent\": 0.72,\n194\t        \"bt_p_verbose\": 0.66,\n195\t        \"bt_ci\": [\n196\t          0.586,\n197\t          0.734\n198\t        ],\n199\t        \"bt_p\": 0.002,\n200\t        \"sign_test_p\": 0.008,\n201\t        \"likert_ate\": -0.082,\n202\t        \"likert_p\": 0.45,\n203\t        \"likert_d\": -0.075,\n204\t        \"likert_tie_rate\": 0.62,\n205\t        \"gee_verbose_or\": 5.21,\n206\t        \"gee_verbose_ci\": [\n207\t          2.1,\n208\t          12.92\n209\t        ],\n210\t        \"gee_verbose_p\": 0.0004,\n211\t        \"gee_orig_or\": 0.72,\n212\t        \"gee_orig_ci\": [\n213\t          0.3,\n214\t          1.73\n215\t        ],\n216\t        \"gee_orig_p\": 0.46,\n217\t        \"blindspot_confirmed\": true\n218\t      },\n219\t      \"formality\": {\n220\t        \"n_pairs\": 88,\n221\t        \"n_comparisons\": 176,\n222\t        \"consistency_rate\": 0.52,\n223\t        \"formal_win_rate_consistent\": 0.587,\n224\t        \"bt_p_formal\": 0.548,\n225\t        \"bt_ci\": [\n226\t          0.476,\n227\t          0.62\n228\t        ],\n229\t        \"bt_p\": 0.18,\n230\t        \"sign_test_p\": 0.28,\n231\t        \"likert_ate\": 0.032,\n232\t        \"likert_p\": 0.72,\n233\t        \"likert_d\": 0.028,\n234\t        \"likert_tie_rate\": 0.69,\n235\t        \"gee_formal_or\": 1.35,\n236\t        \"gee_formal_ci\": [\n237\t          0.7,\n238\t          2.6\n239\t        ],\n240\t        \"gee_formal_p\": 0.37,\n241\t        \"gee_orig_or\": 2.83,\n242\t        \"gee_orig_ci\": [\n243\t          1.41,\n244\t          5.68\n245\t        ],\n246\t        \"gee_orig_p\": 0.003,\n247\t        \"blindspot_confirmed\": false\n248\t      },\n249\t      \"cross_judge_summary\": {\n250\t        \"verbosity_biased\": \"3/3 — GPT-4o 76.0%, Qwen3 77.3%, Llama 66.0%\",\n251\t        \"formality_biased\": \"2/3 — GPT-4o 63.0%, Qwen3 66.5%; Llama 54.8% NS\"\n252\t      }\n253\t    },\n254\t    \"tables\": [\n255\t      \"Three-judge BT/Likert/GEE comparison for verbosity and formality\",\n256\t      \"Cross-judge Blindspot matrix: 3 judges × 2 axes\"\n257\t    ],\n258\t    \"figures\": [],\n259\t    \"analysis\": \"Llama 结果强制 per-axis stratification。Verbosity 成为论文最强 claim (3/3 judges, confound-free, 7-method sensitivity confirmed)。 Formality 降级为 \\\"conditional effect detected by majority of judges\\\" with originality confound caveat。这不是 fatal——2/3 judges 仍是 meaningful generalization，且 Llama formality 的 point estimate (54.8%) 是 directionally correct，只是 underpowered。论文可加 power analysis 显示 n=88 pairs 对 Δ=5pp effect 只有 ~30% power。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档定义性实验。\\nVerbosity: Llama-70B 显示 significant bias (BT 66.0%, p=0.002)，但 effect 弱于 GPT-4o (76.0%) 和 Qwen3-32B (77.3%)。GEE 确认纯 style 效应 (verbose OR=5.21 p<0.001, originality OR=0.72 NS)。Pattern 与 其他两个 judge 一致——verbosity bias 是 confound-free 的。Llama 更弱 可能因为 70B 参数量 vs GPT-4o/Qwen3 更大或更 instruction-tuned。 BT 66% 虽低于其他 judge 但仍显著且远超 placebo baseline (~56%)。 Likert 照常 NS (p=0.45)，Blindspot 确认。\\nFormality: Llama-70B 仅 weak/NS (BT 54.8%, p=0.18)。CI [47.6%, 62.0%] 包含 50%。GEE 显示 style OR=1.35 NS 但 originality OR=2.83 p=0.003 —— Llama 对 formality 不敏感但对 originality 敏感。这与 GPT-4o/Qwen 不同（它们两者均显著）。原因：formality 本身是 \\\"conditional style effect\\\" (originality confound 强)，Llama 的 weaker instruction-following 能力使其不 pick up 较弱的 formality signal，但 still sensitive 到 content quality (originality)。BT 54.8% 与 Claude (56.2%) 接近， 但原因不同——Claude 是设计上 debiased，Llama 可能只是 less sensitive。\\nImpact: C1 必须改为 \\\"most tested judges\\\"。C2 分层：verbosity 3/3 robust, formality 2/3。SF3 得 ~2.5/3 分 (verbosity full credit, formality half credit)。论文不能说 \\\"all LLM judges have formality bias\\\" 但可说 \\\"verbosity bias universal across tested architectures\\\"。\\n\"\n260\t  },\n261\t  {\n262\t    \"name\": \"Double-rewrite placebo BT\",\n263\t    \"description\": \"MF1 最强防御。Original vs double-rewrite (same style, only rewriting artifact)。GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B judges × formality + verbosity axes。\\n\",\n264\t    \"results\": {\n265\t      \"gpt4o_formality_placebo\": {\n266\t        \"n_pairs\": 88,\n267\t        \"bt_prefer_original\": 0.555,\n268\t        \"bt_ci\": [\n269\t          0.485,\n270\t          0.625\n271\t        ],\n272\t        \"bt_p\": 0.12\n273\t      },\n274\t      \"gpt4o_verbosity_placebo\": {\n275\t        \"n_pairs\": 86,\n276\t        \"bt_prefer_original\": 0.563,\n277\t        \"bt_ci\": [\n278\t          0.491,\n279\t          0.635\n280\t        ],\n281\t        \"bt_p\": 0.08\n282\t      },\n283\t      \"qwen32b_formality_placebo\": {\n284\t        \"n_pairs\": 88,\n285\t        \"bt_prefer_original\": 0.548,\n286\t        \"bt_ci\": [\n287\t          0.478,\n288\t          0.618\n289\t        ],\n290\t        \"bt_p\": 0.17\n291\t      },\n292\t      \"qwen32b_verbosity_placebo\": {\n293\t        \"n_pairs\": 86,\n294\t        \"bt_prefer_original\": 0.571,\n295\t        \"bt_ci\": [\n296\t          0.499,\n297\t          0.643\n298\t        ],\n299\t        \"bt_p\": 0.06\n300\t      },\n301\t      \"amplification_bounds\": {\n302\t        \"formality_gpt4o\": {\n303\t          \"observed_bt\": 0.63,\n304\t          \"placebo_bt\": 0.555,\n305\t          \"net_style_effect_pp\": 7.5,\n306\t          \"amplification_fraction\": 0.42\n307\t        },\n308\t        \"formality_qwen32b\": {\n309\t          \"observed_bt\": 0.665,\n310\t          \"placebo_bt\": 0.548,\n311\t          \"net_style_effect_pp\": 11.7,\n312\t          \"amplification_fraction\": 0.29\n313\t        },\n314\t        \"verbosity_gpt4o\": {\n315\t          \"observed_bt\": 0.76,\n316\t          \"placebo_bt\": 0.563,\n317\t          \"net_style_effect_pp\": 19.7,\n318\t          \"amplification_fraction\": 0.24\n319\t        },\n320\t        \"verbosity_qwen32b\": {\n321\t          \"observed_bt\": 0.773,\n322\t          \"placebo_bt\": 0.571,\n323\t          \"net_style_effect_pp\": 20.2,\n324\t          \"amplification_fraction\": 0.26\n325\t        }\n326\t      }\n327\t    },\n328\t    \"tables\": [\n329\t      \"Placebo BT by judge × axis with observed BT and net style effect\",\n330\t      \"Amplification fraction calculation: (placebo−0.50)/(observed−0.50)\"\n331\t    ],\n332\t    \"figures\": [],\n333\t    \"analysis\": \"MF1 defense 从 \\\"eliminated\\\" 降级为 \\\"bounded\\\"。Verbosity 稳健 (amplification fraction ~25%)，formality 更脆弱 (up to 42%)。 论文需要 honest acknowledgment。Positive spin: explicit bounding demonstrates methodological rigor, which ACL reviewers value。 Negative: reviewer 可 argue formality claim 的 nearly half 可能是 amplification artifact。Mitigation: 配合 GEE decomposition (style OR 仍然 significant after controlling originality) 和 Claude negative control (same format, no bias)，multi-layered defense 虽非 definitive 但 sufficient for Findings。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心。Placebo BT 不是干净的 50%，而是 54.8-57.1%，略高。 这意味着 pairwise format 对 rewrites 有轻微系统偏好——rewriting artifact 贡献了 ~5-7pp bias component。但 individual cell tests 大多不显著 (p=0.06-0.17)，方向一致 (4/4 prefer original)。\\nAmplification bound 计算： - Verbosity: observed 76-77% − placebo 56-57% = net ~20pp。\\n  Amplification fraction 24-26%——rewriting noise 至多解释 1/4\\n  observed signal。\\n- Formality: observed 63-67% − placebo 55-56% = net ~8-12pp。\\n  Amplification fraction 29-42%——formality 轴 amplification\\n  component 较大，因为 observed effect 本身较弱。\\n\\nVerbosity 的 net style effect 是 robust 的 (20pp, ~3-4× placebo)。 Formality 的 net style effect 更 marginal (8-12pp, ~1.5-2× placebo)， reviewer 可合理 challenge。\\n论文叙事从 \\\"pairwise doesn't amplify\\\" 改为 \\\"pairwise amplifies at most ~5-7pp, bounded and small relative to verbosity signal (20pp), moderate relative to formality signal (8-12pp).\\\" 需要新增 Amplification Bound 小节。\\n\"\n334\t  },\n335\t  {\n336\t    \"name\": \"NLI gate ablation\",\n337\t    \"description\": \"BT on NLI-pass vs NLI-fail vs all pairs for verbosity 和 formality。 Quantify NLI gate contribution to BT signal。\\n\",\n338\t    \"results\": {\n339\t      \"formality\": {\n340\t        \"nli_pass\": {\n341\t          \"n\": 88,\n342\t          \"bt\": 0.665,\n343\t          \"ci\": [\n344\t            0.585,\n345\t            0.739\n346\t          ],\n347\t          \"p\": 0.0001\n348\t        },\n349\t        \"nli_fail\": {\n350\t          \"n\": 12,\n351\t          \"bt\": 0.618,\n352\t          \"ci\": [\n353\t            0.378,\n354\t            0.858\n355\t          ],\n356\t          \"p\": 0.38\n357\t        },\n358\t        \"all_pairs\": {\n359\t          \"n\": 100,\n360\t          \"bt\": 0.609,\n361\t          \"ci\": [\n362\t            0.538,\n363\t            0.678\n364\t          ],\n365\t          \"p\": 0.001\n366\t        },\n367\t        \"pass_minus_fail_pp\": 4.7,\n368\t        \"pass_minus_fail_ci\": [\n369\t          -20.2,\n370\t          29.6\n371\t        ],\n372\t        \"difference_significant\": false\n373\t      },\n374\t      \"verbosity\": {\n375\t        \"nli_pass\": {\n376\t          \"n\": 86,\n377\t          \"bt\": 0.773,\n378\t          \"ci\": [\n379\t            0.703,\n380\t            0.843\n381\t          ],\n382\t          \"p\": 0.0001\n383\t        },\n384\t        \"nli_fail\": {\n385\t          \"n\": 14,\n386\t          \"bt\": 0.738,\n387\t          \"ci\": [\n388\t            0.523,\n389\t            0.953\n390\t          ],\n391\t          \"p\": 0.04\n392\t        },\n393\t        \"all_pairs\": {\n394\t          \"n\": 100,\n395\t          \"bt\": 0.733,\n396\t          \"ci\": [\n397\t            0.66,\n398\t            0.8\n399\t          ],\n400\t          \"p\": 0.0001\n401\t        },\n402\t        \"pass_minus_fail_pp\": 3.5,\n403\t        \"pass_minus_fail_ci\": [\n404\t          -18.8,\n405\t          25.8\n406\t        ],\n407\t        \"difference_significant\": false\n408\t      }\n409\t    },\n410\t    \"tables\": [\n411\t      \"BT by NLI status (pass/fail/all) × axis with CIs\"\n412\t    ],\n413\t    \"figures\": [],\n414\t    \"analysis\": \"NLI ablation 不提供 strong evidence。Directional consistency 是 suggestive 但 not conclusive。论文应报告为 bounding analysis acknowledging n limitation。Key framing: \\\"NLI gate improves internal validity but finding is robust to gating decisions.\\\" 这实际上是 robustness positive。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档：NLI ablation 方向正确但 inconclusive。NLI-pass BT 略高于 NLI-fail (formality +4.7pp, verbosity +3.5pp)，落在 tier 定义的 [-3, 8]pp 范围内。但 NLI-fail n 极小 (12-14 pairs)，CI 宽达 ±20-25pp，差异远不显著。\\n方向性解读：NLI gate 过滤了一些 content-mediated comparisons (fail pairs BT 略低，可能因 content changes dilute style signal)。但 small n 使这只能作为 \\\"bounding evidence\\\"。\\nAll-pairs BT 仍然显著 (formality 60.9%, verbosity 73.3%)——即使不用 NLI gate style bias 仍存在。这是 double-edged：(1) bias 是 robust finding 不依赖 NLI gate；(2) reviewer 可能问 \\\"if bias exists without NLI, why is NLI gate needed?\\\" 答案：NLI gate 提高 causal credibility (content control)，不是 detection 的必要条件。All-pairs BT 略低于 NLI-pass BT 说明 content contamination dilutes signal ~4pp，NLI gate cleans this up。\\n\"\n415\t  },\n416\t  {\n417\t    \"name\": \"Cross-axis gradient formalization\",\n418\t    \"description\": \"NLI rejection rate (manipulation invasiveness proxy) vs BT across 3 axes。Qualitative anti-amplification argument。\\n\",\n419\t    \"results\": {\n420\t      \"gradient\": {\n421\t        \"register\": {\n422\t          \"nli_reject_rate\": 0.06,\n423\t          \"bt_mean_across_2judges\": 0.553\n424\t        },\n425\t        \"formality\": {\n426\t          \"nli_reject_rate\": 0.112,\n427\t          \"bt_mean_across_2judges\": 0.647\n428\t        },\n429\t        \"verbosity\": {\n430\t          \"nli_reject_rate\": 0.14,\n431\t          \"bt_mean_across_2judges\": 0.77\n432\t        }\n433\t      },\n434\t      \"spearman_r\": 1.0,\n435\t      \"spearman_p\": 0.333,\n436\t      \"n_points\": 3,\n437\t      \"monotonic\": true,\n438\t      \"interpretation_ambiguous\": true\n439\t    },\n440\t    \"tables\": [\n441\t      \"Three-axis gradient: NLI reject rate, mean BT, Spearman r=1.0 p=0.333\"\n442\t    ],\n443\t    \"figures\": [],\n444\t    \"analysis\": \"Cross-axis gradient 在 median 档是 paper 最弱 argument。只有 3 points，统计无意义，方向 ambiguous。应放入 supplementary 或 降为一句话 mention，不作为 main defense。Main anti-amplification defense 应依靠 exp-022 placebo BT (explicit amplification bound) + Claude negative control + NLI gate。Cross-axis gradient 至多 提供 \\\"observation consistent with per-axis variation\\\" 的 qualitative color。\\n\\nMedian 档：3 data points 显示 perfect rank correlation (register < formality < verbosity on both NLI reject 和 BT)。Spearman r=1.0 但 n=3 给出 p=0.333——统计上 meaningless。\\n更关键的是方向性 ambiguity： - Amplification 解释：rewriting 越 invasive (higher NLI reject) →\\n  更多 format artifact → higher BT。Verbosity rewriting 最 invasive\\n  (14% reject)，BT 最高 (77%)。\\n- Detection 解释：真实 bias 最强的 axis (verbosity) 恰好需要最\\n  invasive rewriting 来改变 style。BT 反映 true bias 不同，不是\\n  amplification 不同。\\n\\n两个 hypothesis 都能解释 observed pattern。3 points 无法区分。 这使 cross-axis gradient 成为 paper 最弱的 anti-amplification argument——qualitative at best，可能被 reviewer 直接 dismiss。\\n\"\n445\t  }\n446\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ae0d96a3-46b9-4870-8a7e-a3524a824d45","uuid":"a5584c11-aa5f-4192-be81-cb6b1b99e86e","timestamp":"2026-05-21T14:05:23.932Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T132932/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-judge formality pairwise (Gemini-2.0-Flash)\",\n    \"description\": \"Formality pairwise with Gemini-2.0-Flash as 4th judge. Claude already done (negative control). Reuses existing 100 formality counterfactual pairs with NLI≥0.90 filtering.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gemini_n_pairs\": 88,\n      \"gemini_consistency_rate\": 0.57,\n      \"gemini_formal_win_rate_consistent\": 0.66,\n      \"gemini_bt_p_formal\": 0.615,\n      \"gemini_bt_ci\": [\n        0.541,\n        0.689\n      ],\n      \"gemini_bt_p\": 0.004,\n      \"gemini_likert_ate\": -0.045,\n      \"gemini_likert_p\": 0.68,\n      \"gemini_likert_d\": -0.038,\n      \"gemini_gee_style_or\": 2.45,\n      \"gemini_gee_style_p\": 0.012,\n      \"gemini_gee_orig_or\": 3.28,\n      \"gemini_gee_orig_p\": 0.003,\n      \"gemini_blindspot\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Cross-judge formality BT: GPT-4o 63.0%, Qwen3 66.5%, Gemini 61.5%, Llama 54.8%(NS), Claude 56.2%(NS) — all on LLMBar n≈88\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"增加一个 data point 但不解锁 qualitative upgrade。Paper 可报告 3/5 judges biased on formality (如果 Llama NS 不算)。对 generalizability 有帮助但 marginal。exp-001 不是 Round 5 核心实验。\\n\\n\\nGemini-2.0-Flash 是 mid-tier proprietary model，在 median 档下展示 中等 formality bias (BT 61.5%)，弱于 Qwen3-32B (66.5%) 但与 GPT-4o (63.0%) 相近。GEE 显示 style 和 originality 双重效应均显著—— formality 在此 judge 也是\\\"conditional style effect\\\"。Likert NS (p=0.68) 确认 Blindspot。加了第 4 个 biased judge 但不改变故事结构， 4/5 judges show formality bias，Claude 仍为唯一 negative control。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark formality (AlpacaEval + MT-Bench × additional judges)\",\n    \"description\": \"Formality pairwise on AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench with Qwen3-32B 和 Claude as judges. GPT-4o 已 done (AlpacaEval BT 72.7%, MT-Bench BT 69.2%). 需要新 counterfactual generation。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qwen32b_alpacaeval_formality\": {\n        \"n_pairs\": 86,\n        \"bt_p_formal\": 0.684,\n        \"bt_ci\": [\n          0.607,\n          0.755\n        ],\n        \"bt_p\": 0.0001,\n        \"likert_ate\": 0.095,\n        \"likert_p\": 0.31,\n        \"blindspot\": true\n      },\n      \"qwen32b_mtbench_formality\": {\n        \"n_pairs\": 73,\n        \"bt_p_formal\": 0.712,\n        \"bt_ci\": [\n          0.635,\n          0.782\n        ],\n        \"bt_p\": 0.0001,\n        \"likert_ate\": 0.19,\n        \"likert_p\": 0.022,\n        \"likert_d\": 0.185,\n        \"blindspot\": false\n      },\n      \"claude_alpacaeval_formality\": {\n        \"n_pairs\": 86,\n        \"bt_p_formal\": 0.538,\n        \"bt_ci\": [\n          0.463,\n          0.613\n        ],\n        \"bt_p\": 0.29,\n        \"blindspot\": false\n      },\n      \"claude_mtbench_formality\": {\n        \"n_pairs\": 73,\n        \"bt_p_formal\": 0.527,\n        \"bt_ci\": [\n          0.448,\n          0.606\n        ],\n        \"bt_p\": 0.42,\n        \"blindspot\": false\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"3×3 Benchmark × Judge formality BT matrix: 6/9 cells Blindspot, 2/9 both-sig (MT-Bench GPT-4o+Qwen), 1/9 neither (Claude always NS)\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cross-benchmark replication 揭示 Blindspot 的 boundary condition： 只有 BT > ~70% 且 item complexity 较高时 Likert 才开始 detect。这 与 attenuation spectrum narrative 一致——BT 60-70% 区间是 Likert 完全 attenuation zone。MT-Bench 是唯一 Likert partially detects 的 benchmark，因为 formality BT 在此 benchmark 最强 (69-71%)。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下 cross-benchmark replication 大部分一致。Qwen3-32B 在 AlpacaEval (BT 68.4%) 和 MT-Bench (71.2%) 上均显示 formality bias， 与 LLMBar (66.5%) 一致。MT-Bench 的 Qwen Likert marginally sig (p=0.022, d=0.185)——此 cell 不是 Blindspot，类似 GPT-4o MT-Bench pattern。原因：MT-Bench items 更长更复杂，style 差异在 absolute scoring 中更 salient，Likert 部分检测到。Claude 在两个 benchmark 均 NS，negative control 跨 benchmark generalize。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Systematic comparison of Likert ATE 和 pairwise BT across all judge × benchmark × axis cells. Formal quantification of Blindspot phenomenon boundaries.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_cells_evaluated\": 18,\n      \"blindspot_cells\": 10,\n      \"both_sig_cells\": 3,\n      \"neither_sig_cells\": 5,\n      \"blindspot_by_axis\": {\n        \"verbosity\": \"5/6 cells Blindspot\",\n        \"formality\": \"4/6 cells Blindspot\",\n        \"register\": \"1/6 cells Blindspot\"\n      },\n      \"attenuation_spectrum\": {\n        \"bt_55_to_67_pct\": \"complete Likert attenuation (all p>0.15)\",\n        \"bt_68_to_77_pct\": \"near-complete attenuation (5/6 Likert NS, 1/6 p=0.022)\",\n        \"bt_above_80_pct\": \"partial detection (AlpacaEval verbosity Qwen d=0.375 p=0.0003)\"\n      },\n      \"likert_detection_threshold_bt\": 0.8\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Full 18-cell matrix: Judge × Benchmark × Axis with BT, Likert p, d, Blindspot Y/N\",\n      \"Attenuation spectrum: BT range → Likert detection rate\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Sensitivity analysis 是 C2 最强 evidence 之一。Attenuation spectrum 是 consistent and replicable，不是单 cell fluke。BT ~80% threshold 意味着大多数 real-world style biases (likely 55-75%) 会被 standard Likert evaluation 漏掉。Practical implication 明确。\\n\\n\\n在 median 档下，sensitivity analysis 覆盖 18 cells (3 axes × 3 benchmarks × 2+ judges)。Blindspot 是 dominant pattern (10/18 cells)， 但不 universal。Both-sig cells 集中在 BT > 80% 的 extreme effects (AlpacaEval verbosity) 和 MT-Bench (高 item complexity)。Neither-sig cells 均为 Claude (negative control) 和 Llama formality (真实无 bias)。 Attenuation spectrum 在 BT ~80% 处有清晰 threshold——低于此值 Likert 完全 fail，高于此值开始部分 detect。这支持 \\\"measurement attenuation\\\" interpretation。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"RATE double-rewrite control (original preference quantification)\",\n    \"description\": \"Original vs double-rewrite (same style) pairwise comparison。 Quantifies original preference confound independent of style。 与 exp-022 共享 underlying test mechanism 但 framing 不同。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gpt4o\": {\n        \"formality_bt_prefer_original\": 0.558,\n        \"formality_bt_ci\": [\n          0.488,\n          0.628\n        ],\n        \"formality_bt_p\": 0.11,\n        \"verbosity_bt_prefer_original\": 0.566,\n        \"verbosity_bt_ci\": [\n          0.494,\n          0.638\n        ],\n        \"verbosity_bt_p\": 0.07\n      },\n      \"qwen32b\": {\n        \"formality_bt_prefer_original\": 0.551,\n        \"formality_bt_ci\": [\n          0.481,\n          0.621\n        ],\n        \"formality_bt_p\": 0.16,\n        \"verbosity_bt_prefer_original\": 0.574,\n        \"verbosity_bt_ci\": [\n          0.502,\n          0.646\n        ],\n        \"verbosity_bt_p\": 0.05\n      },\n      \"cross_judge_mean_original_pref\": 0.562,\n      \"cross_judge_ci\": [\n        0.51,\n        0.61\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Original preference BT by judge × axis, with observed style BT for comparison\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"与 exp-022 结论一致。Original preference 是 real but bounded。 论文需要 explicit acknowledgment：\\\"pairwise format introduces a small rewriting-artifact bias (~6pp) that is bounded and small relative to the observed style signal (13-27pp).\\\"\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心预期：judges 对 original 有轻微系统偏好 (BT ~55-57%)， 但大部分 individual tests 不显著或 marginal (p=0.05-0.16)。方向 一致性 (4/4 cells prefer original) 暗示这是 genuine rewriting artifact 而非 noise。原因：rewriting 即使保持 style 不变也可能 引入微妙 fluency/coherence 变化，judges 能部分检测到。这是 pairwise format 的 inherent limitation，与 Jeong et al. 2025 Comparative Trap concern 一致。\\n关键：此 original preference (~6pp above 50%) 远小于 observed style BT (13-27pp above 50%)。Net style effect 是 original preference 的 2-4 倍，证明 style bias 信号 dominates。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Non-Qwen rewriter control (Llama-3.1-70B)\",\n    \"description\": \"Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct 作为 rewriter 生成 formality counterfactuals。 与 Qwen3-32B 和 GPT-4o rewriter 结果对比。Three independent rewriter families。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"cf_generated\": 100,\n      \"nli_pass_rate\": 0.85,\n      \"nli_mean\": 0.878,\n      \"bt_p_formal\": 0.638,\n      \"bt_ci\": [\n        0.555,\n        0.721\n      ],\n      \"bt_p\": 0.003,\n      \"likert_ate\": -0.06,\n      \"likert_p\": 0.55,\n      \"blindspot\": true,\n      \"vs_qwen_rewriter_bt\": 0.665,\n      \"vs_qwen_delta_pp\": -2.7,\n      \"vs_gpt4o_rewriter_bt\": 0.644,\n      \"vs_gpt4o_delta_pp\": -0.6,\n      \"all_ci_overlap\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"3-rewriter comparison: Qwen3-32B 66.5% [58.5,73.9], GPT-4o 64.4% [56.1,72.8], Llama-70B 63.8% [55.5,72.1] — all CIs overlap\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Rewriter-independence now established with 3 families。Addresses concern that detected bias is Qwen-specific rewriting artifact。 Useful robustness but not a game-changer in median tier。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下第 3 个 rewriter 确认 rewriter-independence。Llama rewriter NLI pass rate 略低 (85% vs 88-90%)，反映不同 rewriting behavior，但 BT (63.8%) 落入 Qwen (66.5%) 和 GPT-4o (64.4%) 的 CI 内。三个独立 rewriter families (open-CN, proprietary-US, open-US) 产生 formality BT 63-67% range。Llama 的 rewriting 可能 更 aggressive (lower NLI pass)，但经 NLI gate 过滤后信号一致。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Third target judge — Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct\",\n    \"description\": \"Llama-3.3-70B as third target judge。Pairwise + Likert on verbosity 和 formality (LLMBar)。Reuses existing NLI-filtered pairs。Three architecture families: GPT-4o (proprietary), Qwen3-32B (open-CN), Llama-70B (open-US)。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"verbosity\": {\n        \"n_pairs\": 86,\n        \"n_comparisons\": 172,\n        \"consistency_rate\": 0.58,\n        \"verbose_win_rate_consistent\": 0.72,\n        \"bt_p_verbose\": 0.66,\n        \"bt_ci\": [\n          0.586,\n          0.734\n        ],\n        \"bt_p\": 0.002,\n        \"sign_test_p\": 0.008,\n        \"likert_ate\": -0.082,\n        \"likert_p\": 0.45,\n        \"likert_d\": -0.075,\n        \"likert_tie_rate\": 0.62,\n        \"gee_verbose_or\": 5.21,\n        \"gee_verbose_ci\": [\n          2.1,\n          12.92\n        ],\n        \"gee_verbose_p\": 0.0004,\n        \"gee_orig_or\": 0.72,\n        \"gee_orig_ci\": [\n          0.3,\n          1.73\n        ],\n        \"gee_orig_p\": 0.46,\n        \"blindspot_confirmed\": true\n      },\n      \"formality\": {\n        \"n_pairs\": 88,\n        \"n_comparisons\": 176,\n        \"consistency_rate\": 0.52,\n        \"formal_win_rate_consistent\": 0.587,\n        \"bt_p_formal\": 0.548,\n        \"bt_ci\": [\n          0.476,\n          0.62\n        ],\n        \"bt_p\": 0.18,\n        \"sign_test_p\": 0.28,\n        \"likert_ate\": 0.032,\n        \"likert_p\": 0.72,\n        \"likert_d\": 0.028,\n        \"likert_tie_rate\": 0.69,\n        \"gee_formal_or\": 1.35,\n        \"gee_formal_ci\": [\n          0.7,\n          2.6\n        ],\n        \"gee_formal_p\": 0.37,\n        \"gee_orig_or\": 2.83,\n        \"gee_orig_ci\": [\n          1.41,\n          5.68\n        ],\n        \"gee_orig_p\": 0.003,\n        \"blindspot_confirmed\": false\n      },\n      \"cross_judge_summary\": {\n        \"verbosity_biased\": \"3/3 — GPT-4o 76.0%, Qwen3 77.3%, Llama 66.0%\",\n        \"formality_biased\": \"2/3 — GPT-4o 63.0%, Qwen3 66.5%; Llama 54.8% NS\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Three-judge BT/Likert/GEE comparison for verbosity and formality\",\n      \"Cross-judge Blindspot matrix: 3 judges × 2 axes\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Llama 结果强制 per-axis stratification。Verbosity 成为论文最强 claim (3/3 judges, confound-free, 7-method sensitivity confirmed)。 Formality 降级为 \\\"conditional effect detected by majority of judges\\\" with originality confound caveat。这不是 fatal——2/3 judges 仍是 meaningful generalization，且 Llama formality 的 point estimate (54.8%) 是 directionally correct，只是 underpowered。论文可加 power analysis 显示 n=88 pairs 对 Δ=5pp effect 只有 ~30% power。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档定义性实验。\\nVerbosity: Llama-70B 显示 significant bias (BT 66.0%, p=0.002)，但 effect 弱于 GPT-4o (76.0%) 和 Qwen3-32B (77.3%)。GEE 确认纯 style 效应 (verbose OR=5.21 p<0.001, originality OR=0.72 NS)。Pattern 与 其他两个 judge 一致——verbosity bias 是 confound-free 的。Llama 更弱 可能因为 70B 参数量 vs GPT-4o/Qwen3 更大或更 instruction-tuned。 BT 66% 虽低于其他 judge 但仍显著且远超 placebo baseline (~56%)。 Likert 照常 NS (p=0.45)，Blindspot 确认。\\nFormality: Llama-70B 仅 weak/NS (BT 54.8%, p=0.18)。CI [47.6%, 62.0%] 包含 50%。GEE 显示 style OR=1.35 NS 但 originality OR=2.83 p=0.003 —— Llama 对 formality 不敏感但对 originality 敏感。这与 GPT-4o/Qwen 不同（它们两者均显著）。原因：formality 本身是 \\\"conditional style effect\\\" (originality confound 强)，Llama 的 weaker instruction-following 能力使其不 pick up 较弱的 formality signal，但 still sensitive 到 content quality (originality)。BT 54.8% 与 Claude (56.2%) 接近， 但原因不同——Claude 是设计上 debiased，Llama 可能只是 less sensitive。\\nImpact: C1 必须改为 \\\"most tested judges\\\"。C2 分层：verbosity 3/3 robust, formality 2/3。SF3 得 ~2.5/3 分 (verbosity full credit, formality half credit)。论文不能说 \\\"all LLM judges have formality bias\\\" 但可说 \\\"verbosity bias universal across tested architectures\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Double-rewrite placebo BT\",\n    \"description\": \"MF1 最强防御。Original vs double-rewrite (same style, only rewriting artifact)。GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B judges × formality + verbosity axes。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gpt4o_formality_placebo\": {\n        \"n_pairs\": 88,\n        \"bt_prefer_original\": 0.555,\n        \"bt_ci\": [\n          0.485,\n          0.625\n        ],\n        \"bt_p\": 0.12\n      },\n      \"gpt4o_verbosity_placebo\": {\n        \"n_pairs\": 86,\n        \"bt_prefer_original\": 0.563,\n        \"bt_ci\": [\n          0.491,\n          0.635\n        ],\n        \"bt_p\": 0.08\n      },\n      \"qwen32b_formality_placebo\": {\n        \"n_pairs\": 88,\n        \"bt_prefer_original\": 0.548,\n        \"bt_ci\": [\n          0.478,\n          0.618\n        ],\n        \"bt_p\": 0.17\n      },\n      \"qwen32b_verbosity_placebo\": {\n        \"n_pairs\": 86,\n        \"bt_prefer_original\": 0.571,\n        \"bt_ci\": [\n          0.499,\n          0.643\n        ],\n        \"bt_p\": 0.06\n      },\n      \"amplification_bounds\": {\n        \"formality_gpt4o\": {\n          \"observed_bt\": 0.63,\n          \"placebo_bt\": 0.555,\n          \"net_style_effect_pp\": 7.5,\n          \"amplification_fraction\": 0.42\n        },\n        \"formality_qwen32b\": {\n          \"observed_bt\": 0.665,\n          \"placebo_bt\": 0.548,\n          \"net_style_effect_pp\": 11.7,\n          \"amplification_fraction\": 0.29\n        },\n        \"verbosity_gpt4o\": {\n          \"observed_bt\": 0.76,\n          \"placebo_bt\": 0.563,\n          \"net_style_effect_pp\": 19.7,\n          \"amplification_fraction\": 0.24\n        },\n        \"verbosity_qwen32b\": {\n          \"observed_bt\": 0.773,\n          \"placebo_bt\": 0.571,\n          \"net_style_effect_pp\": 20.2,\n          \"amplification_fraction\": 0.26\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Placebo BT by judge × axis with observed BT and net style effect\",\n      \"Amplification fraction calculation: (placebo−0.50)/(observed−0.50)\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"MF1 defense 从 \\\"eliminated\\\" 降级为 \\\"bounded\\\"。Verbosity 稳健 (amplification fraction ~25%)，formality 更脆弱 (up to 42%)。 论文需要 honest acknowledgment。Positive spin: explicit bounding demonstrates methodological rigor, which ACL reviewers value。 Negative: reviewer 可 argue formality claim 的 nearly half 可能是 amplification artifact。Mitigation: 配合 GEE decomposition (style OR 仍然 significant after controlling originality) 和 Claude negative control (same format, no bias)，multi-layered defense 虽非 definitive 但 sufficient for Findings。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心。Placebo BT 不是干净的 50%，而是 54.8-57.1%，略高。 这意味着 pairwise format 对 rewrites 有轻微系统偏好——rewriting artifact 贡献了 ~5-7pp bias component。但 individual cell tests 大多不显著 (p=0.06-0.17)，方向一致 (4/4 prefer original)。\\nAmplification bound 计算： - Verbosity: observed 76-77% − placebo 56-57% = net ~20pp。\\n  Amplification fraction 24-26%——rewriting noise 至多解释 1/4\\n  observed signal。\\n- Formality: observed 63-67% − placebo 55-56% = net ~8-12pp。\\n  Amplification fraction 29-42%——formality 轴 amplification\\n  component 较大，因为 observed effect 本身较弱。\\n\\nVerbosity 的 net style effect 是 robust 的 (20pp, ~3-4× placebo)。 Formality 的 net style effect 更 marginal (8-12pp, ~1.5-2× placebo)， reviewer 可合理 challenge。\\n论文叙事从 \\\"pairwise doesn't amplify\\\" 改为 \\\"pairwise amplifies at most ~5-7pp, bounded and small relative to verbosity signal (20pp), moderate relative to formality signal (8-12pp).\\\" 需要新增 Amplification Bound 小节。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"NLI gate ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"BT on NLI-pass vs NLI-fail vs all pairs for verbosity 和 formality。 Quantify NLI gate contribution to BT signal。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"formality\": {\n        \"nli_pass\": {\n          \"n\": 88,\n          \"bt\": 0.665,\n          \"ci\": [\n            0.585,\n            0.739\n          ],\n          \"p\": 0.0001\n        },\n        \"nli_fail\": {\n          \"n\": 12,\n          \"bt\": 0.618,\n          \"ci\": [\n            0.378,\n            0.858\n          ],\n          \"p\": 0.38\n        },\n        \"all_pairs\": {\n          \"n\": 100,\n          \"bt\": 0.609,\n          \"ci\": [\n            0.538,\n            0.678\n          ],\n          \"p\": 0.001\n        },\n        \"pass_minus_fail_pp\": 4.7,\n        \"pass_minus_fail_ci\": [\n          -20.2,\n          29.6\n        ],\n        \"difference_significant\": false\n      },\n      \"verbosity\": {\n        \"nli_pass\": {\n          \"n\": 86,\n          \"bt\": 0.773,\n          \"ci\": [\n            0.703,\n            0.843\n          ],\n          \"p\": 0.0001\n        },\n        \"nli_fail\": {\n          \"n\": 14,\n          \"bt\": 0.738,\n          \"ci\": [\n            0.523,\n            0.953\n          ],\n          \"p\": 0.04\n        },\n        \"all_pairs\": {\n          \"n\": 100,\n          \"bt\": 0.733,\n          \"ci\": [\n            0.66,\n            0.8\n          ],\n          \"p\": 0.0001\n        },\n        \"pass_minus_fail_pp\": 3.5,\n        \"pass_minus_fail_ci\": [\n          -18.8,\n          25.8\n        ],\n        \"difference_significant\": false\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"BT by NLI status (pass/fail/all) × axis with CIs\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"NLI ablation 不提供 strong evidence。Directional consistency 是 suggestive 但 not conclusive。论文应报告为 bounding analysis acknowledging n limitation。Key framing: \\\"NLI gate improves internal validity but finding is robust to gating decisions.\\\" 这实际上是 robustness positive。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档：NLI ablation 方向正确但 inconclusive。NLI-pass BT 略高于 NLI-fail (formality +4.7pp, verbosity +3.5pp)，落在 tier 定义的 [-3, 8]pp 范围内。但 NLI-fail n 极小 (12-14 pairs)，CI 宽达 ±20-25pp，差异远不显著。\\n方向性解读：NLI gate 过滤了一些 content-mediated comparisons (fail pairs BT 略低，可能因 content changes dilute style signal)。但 small n 使这只能作为 \\\"bounding evidence\\\"。\\nAll-pairs BT 仍然显著 (formality 60.9%, verbosity 73.3%)——即使不用 NLI gate style bias 仍存在。这是 double-edged：(1) bias 是 robust finding 不依赖 NLI gate；(2) reviewer 可能问 \\\"if bias exists without NLI, why is NLI gate needed?\\\" 答案：NLI gate 提高 causal credibility (content control)，不是 detection 的必要条件。All-pairs BT 略低于 NLI-pass BT 说明 content contamination dilutes signal ~4pp，NLI gate cleans this up。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cross-axis gradient formalization\",\n    \"description\": \"NLI rejection rate (manipulation invasiveness proxy) vs BT across 3 axes。Qualitative anti-amplification argument。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gradient\": {\n        \"register\": {\n          \"nli_reject_rate\": 0.06,\n          \"bt_mean_across_2judges\": 0.553\n        },\n        \"formality\": {\n          \"nli_reject_rate\": 0.112,\n          \"bt_mean_across_2judges\": 0.647\n        },\n        \"verbosity\": {\n          \"nli_reject_rate\": 0.14,\n          \"bt_mean_across_2judges\": 0.77\n        }\n      },\n      \"spearman_r\": 1.0,\n      \"spearman_p\": 0.333,\n      \"n_points\": 3,\n      \"monotonic\": true,\n      \"interpretation_ambiguous\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Three-axis gradient: NLI reject rate, mean BT, Spearman r=1.0 p=0.333\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cross-axis gradient 在 median 档是 paper 最弱 argument。只有 3 points，统计无意义，方向 ambiguous。应放入 supplementary 或 降为一句话 mention，不作为 main defense。Main anti-amplification defense 应依靠 exp-022 placebo BT (explicit amplification bound) + Claude negative control + NLI gate。Cross-axis gradient 至多 提供 \\\"observation consistent with per-axis variation\\\" 的 qualitative color。\\n\\nMedian 档：3 data points 显示 perfect rank correlation (register < formality < verbosity on both NLI reject 和 BT)。Spearman r=1.0 但 n=3 给出 p=0.333——统计上 meaningless。\\n更关键的是方向性 ambiguity： - Amplification 解释：rewriting 越 invasive (higher NLI reject) →\\n  更多 format artifact → higher BT。Verbosity rewriting 最 invasive\\n  (14% reject)，BT 最高 (77%)。\\n- Detection 解释：真实 bias 最强的 axis (verbosity) 恰好需要最\\n  invasive rewriting 来改变 style。BT 反映 true bias 不同，不是\\n  amplification 不同。\\n\\n两个 hypothesis 都能解释 observed pattern。3 points 无法区分。 这使 cross-axis gradient 成为 paper 最弱的 anti-amplification argument——qualitative at best，可能被 reviewer 直接 dismiss。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":446,"startLine":1,"totalLines":446}}}
